messages:
Nina Park: Quick FYI from customer support: an app using our browser SDK borked when a user pasted a string with multiple emoji into the prompt. The stream split an emoji (multi-codepoint) across chunks and the app JSON.parse failed mid-stream.

Owen Li: emoji are nasty because they can be multi-codepoint and encoded across multiple UTF-8 bytes. Are we using TextDecoder with {stream:true} in the browser SDK?

Nina Park: the sample app used `decoder.decode(chunk)` per chunk and then appended to a buffer. That loses decoder state and produces replacement chars or truncation.

Priya Desai: We should standardize the client-side pattern in JS SDK and sample apps: 
- Create a single `const decoder = new TextDecoder();` and call `decoder.decode(chunk, {stream:true})` for every chunk. 
- Keep a `leftover` string/bytes for partial event frames. 
- Split events by SSE delimiter (`\n\n`) or by our event sentinel, and only JSON.parse completed frames.

Owen Li: also add a diagnostic emission when a stream ends with leftover bytes: `sdk.on('stream_incomplete', {bytes: base64(leftover), reason})`. That will help customers debug split/emoji cases.

Nina Park: customer also hit a resume case: they backgrounded the tab, network flapped, then reopened and retried. Our client auto-retried the full streaming request and the app created duplicate side effects. They wanted a safe default.

Priya Desai: Default should be `autoRetryStreaming: 'none'`. If teams want resume, they need to opt-in and use `resumeFrom(token)` with server-side resume window. We'll add SDK API: `stream({autoRetry:'none'|'resume', onEvent, onError})`.

Owen Li: protocol side: include `X-Resume-Token` in SSE comment or an event `: resume-token: <token>` so clients can record `last_event_id`. Server can accept `Last-Event-ID` header on reconnect. Keep resume window short (30s) and best-effort for memory saving.

Nina Park: error handling: when mid-stream auth happens (proxy inserts HTML 401 body), browsers will hand the HTML as chunk text. We should detect if the chunk starts with `<` or `<!doctype` and surface a clear `AuthError: status=401, body_snippet='<...>'` rather than trying to parse as JSON.

Priya Desai: SDK change list: 
1) Browser JS: streaming TextDecoder + leftover buffer + delimiter parsing. 
2) Emit `stream_incomplete` with base64 leftover on close/abort. 
3) Surface final status + headers when response ends with non-200 (so apps can distinguish auth vs normal close). 
4) Default autoRetryStreaming: 'none', add resume API and docs.

Owen Li: Tests to add: partial multi-byte sequences (emoji, CJK), HTML injection mid-stream, abort during decode, and resume token flows. Also a small sample snippet in quickstart: "Handling streaming in single-page apps" showing AbortController + onpopstate cleanup.

Nina Park: minimal repro snippet for docs: 
```js
const res = await fetch('/v1/stream', {signal});
const reader = res.body.getReader();
const decoder = new TextDecoder();
let leftover = '';
while(true){
  const {done, value} = await reader.read();
  if(done) break;
  leftover += decoder.decode(value, {stream:true});
  const parts = leftover.split('\n\n');
  leftover = parts.pop(); // last partial
  for(const p of parts){
    handleEvent(JSON.parse(p));
  }
}
if(leftover) emit('stream_incomplete', {bytes: btoa(leftover)});
```

Priya Desai: Action items: 
- Nina: file a tiny sample-app PR updating quickstart + add repro for emoji split (ETA: today)
- Owen: spec SDK API and add tests (ETA: end of week)
- devex-bot: create ticket and link PRs

devex-bot: Created ticket INF-2150 "browser-sdk: handle multi-codepoint emoji split + streaming resume policy" and assigned Nina and Owen. :white_check_mark:

Nina Park: Thanks — I'll add a one-line changelog note telling customers we no longer auto-retry streaming by default. That should reduce duplicated side effects.

Owen Li: good call. I'll land tests for partial UTF-8 sequences and an HTML-error-detector.

Priya Desai: Closing loop: once SDK emits `stream_incomplete` we should include a troubleshooting doc with common causes (navigation, abort, auth proxy) and suggested fixes.
